 **Stack Tecnológico:**\n  - **Next.js 16+** (App Router)\n  - **React 19**\n  - **Tailwind CSS v4** (configuração CSS-first via `@theme` no `globals.css`)\n  - **TypeScript 5+**\n  - **Biome 2+** (linter e formatador ultrarrápido)\n- **Documentação e Regras de Código:** Consulte [`portifolio-app-front/AGENTS.md`](file:///portifolio-app-front/AGENTS.md) e as skills internas em `portifolio-app-front/.agents/skills/`.\n\n---\n\n## 🧭 Regras Obrigatórias para Agentes e Desenvolvedores\n\n1. **O UX é a Fonte da Verdade:**\n   - Antes de criar ou alterar qualquer tela, seção ou componente no front-end (`portifolio-app-front`), os agentes **devem consultar** os arquivos de layout em `portifolio-ux` (em especial o print [`ux-portifolio-preview.png`](file:///portifolio-ux/ux-portifolio-preview.png) e [`portifolio-ux/README.md`](file:///portifolio-ux/README.md)).\n2. **Consistência de Tokens:**\n   - Nunca invente cores ou tamanhos arbitrários no código. Utilize rigorosamente as variáveis de tema declaradas no Tailwind v4 (`--color-bg-dark`, `--color-cyan-glow`, `--color-red-accent`, `--font-orbitron`, `--font-mono`, etc.), que refletem fielmente o design system do UX.\n3. **Harmonia entre UX e Código:**\n   - Se houver necessidade de alterar a estrutura ou vibe de uma seção no código, documente e verifique se o alinhamento com a proposta do UX foi mantido.\n\n</project_instructions>\n\n<project_instructions path=\"C:\\Users\\ruben\\Desktop\\Workspace - AI\\portifolio\\portifolio-ux\\AGENTS.md\">\n# Instruções para Agentes — Pasta `/portifolio-ux`\n\nEsta pasta é o repositório central de **design, UX e especificações visuais** do portfólio de **Rubens Barbosa**.\n\n---\n\n## 📌 Papel Desta Pasta no Projeto\n- O código da aplicação web reside em [`/portifolio-app-front`](file:///portifolio-app-front).\n- Esta pasta (`/portifolio-ux`) armazena o **planejamento do layout**, os wireframes, a identidade visual e as ferramentas de suporte ao design.\n\n---\n\n## 👁️ Como Visualizar o Design\n1. **Visualização Rápida (Print em PNG):**\n   - Inspecione diretamente a imagem renderizada: [`ux-portifolio-preview.png`](file:///portifolio-ux/ux-portifolio-preview.png).\n2. **Documento Nativo (Pencil / pen.dev):**\n   - O arquivo do layout é [`ux-portifolio.pen`](file:///portifolio-ux/ux-portifolio.pen). Ele pode ser aberto no app desktop Pencil ou inspecionado/manipulado via scripts Node.js nesta pasta quando o app estiver em execução.\n\n---\n\n## 📖 Documentação Completa\nConsulte o arquivo [`README.md`](file:///portifolio-ux/README.md) nesta mesma pasta para:\n- Descrição detalhada da vibe estética e da inspiração no carro do *Rocket League*.\n- Mapeamento completo dos tokens de cores e tipografia.\n- Guia explicativo de cada script de automação (`pencil-bridge.js`, `check-tree.js`, `export-preview.js`, etc.).\n\n</project_instructions>\n</project_context>","cwd":"<cwd>\nC:/Users/ruben/Desktop/Workspace - AI/portifolio/portifolio-ux\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1790980152684,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"browser","description":"\nInteract with a real website loaded in the app's integrated browser: open a URL, reproduce a page (or one element) as editable canvas layers, screenshot it, or pull its DOM/screenshot back into the conversation.\n\nUse it to iterate on real designs: import a live page onto the canvas, take inspiration from a site, or close the loop when generating a design — load the generated page, look at it, and refine.\n\nParameters:\n- action (required):\n  - \"load-page\": load \"url\" in the target browser (opening the sidebar if closed and no \"nodeId\" is given). Returns when the load finishes or fails.\n  - \"import-to-canvas\": reproduce the target as editable Pencil layers on the canvas. The response reports the imported top-level frame's id for use with the execute tool. Each imported node's \"context\" field holds the source element's tag, prefixed with its code component name when detected (e.g. \"Card - div\") — useful for locating the element in the code.\n  - \"screenshot-to-canvas\": place a screenshot of the target on the canvas as an image.\n  - \"return-element\": return the target element's DOM and computed styles as text so you can read/reuse it.\n  - \"return-screenshot\": return a screenshot of the target as an image so you can look at it.\n- nodeId: the id of a browser node in the document to drive. When omitted, the tool drives the browser sidebar's own page. Browser nodes are canvas nodes of type \"browser\"; find their ids with get_app_state or batch_get.\n- target (default \"full-page\"): what to act on.\n  - \"full-page\": the whole page.\n  - \"selection\": the element the user picked with the browser's element picker (errors if none).\n  - \"query\": the element resolved from \"querySelector\".\n- querySelector: a CSS selector, required when target is \"query\".\n- url: an http(s) or file URL, required (and only used) when action is \"load-page\".\n\nUsage:\n- Call action \"load-page\" before the other actions so a page is loaded and visible.\n- localhost dev servers usually live-reload: when the page is already loaded, skip \"load-page\" and check the result directly (e.g. \"return-screenshot\"); only if your change is not visible, reload with \"load-page\" and check again.\n- Prefer target \"query\" or \"selection\" over \"full-page\" to keep imports and reads focused.\n- Be careful with \"return-element\" on \"body\"/\"html\" or broad selectors: a whole page's DOM can be huge and overflow the context. Query a specific section (e.g. \"header\", \".pricing\", \"#hero\"), or use \"return-screenshot\" to view the whole page cheaply.\n- \"return-screenshot\" is for you to inspect visually; \"screenshot-to-canvas\" and \"import-to-canvas\" put the result in the user's document.\n- Imported pages land as normal canvas nodes. Do NOT think in CSS/HTML afterwards — treat the result as a design and edit it with the execute tool like any other content.\n\nExamples:\n- Reproduce a hero section as editable layers: {action: \"load-page\", url: \"https://example.com\"}, then {action: \"import-to-canvas\", target: \"query\", querySelector: \"header.hero\"}.\n- Rebuild a component faithfully: {action: \"return-element\", target: \"query\", querySelector: \".pricing-card\"} to read its DOM and styles, then {action: \"return-screenshot\", target: \"query\", querySelector: \".pricing-card\"} to check your own render against it.\n- Close the loop on a locally served generated page: {action: \"load-page\", url: \"http://localhost:3000\"}, then {action: \"return-screenshot\", target: \"full-page\"}.\n","parameters":{"properties":{"action":{"description":"What to do: load-page, import-to-canvas, screenshot-to-canvas, return-element, or return-screenshot.","enum":["load-page","import-to-canvas","screenshot-to-canvas","return-element","return-screenshot"],"type":"string"},"filePath":{"description":"An optional file path to access a .pen file.","type":"string"},"nodeId":{"description":"Id of a browser node in the document to drive. Omit to drive the browser sidebar's own page.","type":"string"},"querySelector":{"description":"A CSS selector executed in the page. Required when target is \"query\".","type":"string"},"target":{"description":"What to act on (default full-page).","enum":["full-page","selection","query"],"type":"string"},"url":{"description":"An http(s) or file URL to load. Used when action is \"load-page\".","type":"string"}},"required":["filePath","action"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"execute","description":"Use get_app_state if you don't have execute documentation","parameters":{"properties":{"editId":{"description":"The id of the failed snippet to patch, as printed in that call's failure message. Send it only together with `edits`, and always use a valid editId that is referencing a failed execute call. Never send it alongside `input`.","type":"string"},"edits":{"description":"When an execute call fails, ALWAYS retry with this instead of resending the snippet in `input`. Each edit replaces `find` with `replace` in the failed snippet, then the patched snippet re-runs from scratch. Edits apply in order: each `find` must match the snippet as already modified by the preceding edits. Requires `editId`; omit `input` when using it. If the patched snippet fails again, keep fixing it with further `edits` under the same editId - `find` must then match the already-patched snippet.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"all":{"description":"Replace every occurrence instead of requiring a unique match.","type":"boolean"},"find":{"description":"Exact text in the failed snippet to replace. Must match exactly once unless `all` is true.","type":"string"},"replace":{"description":"The replacement text.","type":"string"}},"required":["find","replace"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"filePath":{"description":"An optional file path to access a .pen file.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"The JavaScript snippet to execute. Required unless `edits` is provided.","type":"string"}},"required":["filePath"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"get_app_state","description":"Get info about the current state of the pen.dev app., current user selections and other essential information to get started on a task.","parameters":{"properties":{},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"name":"get_style","description":"Load visual style archetypes for working with .pen files. Styles provide configurable fonts, colors, and imagery. Styles do not save variables, they only provide reference values.\n\nUsage:\n1. get_style(): list available styles\n2. get_style({ name }): load style with no params or get required params when required\n3. get_style({ name, params }): load style","parameters":{"properties":{"name":{"description":"Style name from the listing","type":"string"},"params":{"description":"Key-value pairs for required params returned in step 2","properties":{},"type":"object"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"name":"read_skill","description":"Read the pen-dev skill that teaches how to design on the pen.dev canvas.\n\nUsage:\n1. read_skill(): returns the skill's SKILL.md\n2. read_skill({ path }): read a file referenced from SKILL.md (e.g. \"execute.md\", \"guide/web-app.md\")","parameters":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Relative path of a file referenced from SKILL.md. Omit to read SKILL.md itself.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}}]}}
